  "finalText": "All 52 tests pass. Here's what was changed:\n\n### `apps/extension/src/commands.ts` — `runCli`\n\nAdded `statusBar?.render(client)` after `refreshAll()` in all three exit paths (success, failure result, thrown exception). The `finally` block remains as a safety net. This ensures the status bar is always re-rendered from the updated client state immediately after the run completes, rather than relying solely on `refreshAll()` (which may or may not render the status bar depending on the consumer).\n\n| Path | Before | After |\n|------|--------|-------|\n| Success | `lastBuildError = null` → `refreshAll()` | `lastBuildError = null` → `refreshAll()` → **`statusBar?.render(client)`** |\n| Failure | `lastBuildError = msg` → `refreshAll()` | `lastBuildError = msg` → `refreshAll()` → **`statusBar?.render(client)`** |\n| Exception | `lastBuildError = msg` → `refreshAll()` | `lastBuildError = msg` → `refreshAll()` → **`statusBar?.render(client)`** |\n\n### `apps/extension/tests/commands.test.ts`\n\n- Added `statusBar: FakeStatusBarItem` to `Harness` interface\n- `makeHarness` now creates a `StatusBarController` with a `FakeStatusBarItem` and passes it to the `CommandContext`, so the `indexing()` and `render()` calls are exercised\n- `records a build error when the run fails` test now also asserts the status bar shows `\"build failed\"` with the correct tooltip\n- New test: **`shows 'no index' after a successful build on an empty fixture`** — verifies the status bar transitions from `\"indexing…\"` to `\"no index\"` (not stuck) after a successful run on an empty workspace",
